nt depends on the assumption that compute usage remains a reliable proxy for model capability and risk, and that regulators possess the political will to enforce liability. If compute-to-capability scaling laws were to collapse, or if regulatory capture rendered strict liability toothless, the reliance on hardware telemetry would only serve to legitimize dangerous development under the guise of compliance. Despite these risks, a synthesis of hardware-level visibility and strict liability remains the most robust path toward a safer AI ecosystem, shifting the burden of verification from the public back onto the developers.",
